cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SyncAI-Lib-HydraNet: multi-task perception for fixed store CCTV"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: SYNCROBOTIC
repository-code: "https://github.com/Syncrobotic/SyncAI-Lib-HydraNet"
abstract: >-
  A multi-head perception network for fixed store CCTV, answering retail analytics and
  security questions off one camera and one forward pass. A shared RegNetX backbone and
  BiFPN neck feed independent heads — terrain segmentation, traversability, anchor-free
  FCOS object detection and monocular depth — of which each deployment config trains the
  subset it needs. Trained in PyTorch under partial supervision across datasets, so no
  single dataset has to label every task, and exported to ONNX for TensorRT on a Jetson
  Orin. Host-side second-stage analytics turn the boxes into tracks and the tracks into
  events on the floor in metres.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - multi-task learning
  - semantic segmentation
  - object detection
  - traversability
  - cctv
  - retail analytics
  - video surveillance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0 # x-release-please-version
